hadiths[251]{hadithnumber,text}:
"500","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: “Whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah will send ten mercies upon him and forgive ten of his mistakes.”"
"501","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the pulpit. When he stepped on the first step, he said: ""Ameen."" Then when he ascended the second step, he said: ""Ameen."" Then when he ascended the third step, he said: ""Ameen."" The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! We heard you say 'Ameen' three times?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When I ascended the first step, Jibreel came to me and said: 'Wretched is the servant who finds Ramadan and lets it pass without being forgiven.' I said: 'Ameen.' Then he said: 'Wretched is the servant who finds his parents, one or both of them, in old age and does not enter Paradise by serving them.' I said: 'Ameen.' Then he said: 'Wretched is the person in whose presence your name is mentioned and he does not send blessings upon you.' I said: 'Ameen.'"""
"502","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Whoever sends blessings upon me once, Allah sends ten mercies upon him."""
"503","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) ascended the pulpit and said: “Ameen, Ameen, Ameen.” It was said to him: O Messenger of Allah! You did not use to do this before. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Jibreel said to me, ‘May his nose be rubbed in dust, the one who finds his parents or one of them in old age, and yet he does not enter Paradise (by serving them).’ I said: Ameen. Then he said, ‘May his nose be rubbed in dust, the one who witnesses the month of Ramadan and is not forgiven.’ I said: Ameen. Then he said, ‘May his nose be rubbed in dust, the one in whose presence your name is mentioned and he does not send blessings upon you.’ I said: Ameen."
"504","It is narrated from Sayyidah Juwayriyyah bint Harith bin Abi Dhirar (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from her place. This Juwayriyyah is the one whose name was Barrah; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed her name to Juwayriyyah. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out from her place, and he disliked to go to her while her name was Barrah. Then he returned to her after the day had advanced, and she was still sitting as before. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Have you remained sitting here as you were?"" She replied in the affirmative. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""After I left you, I said four phrases three times. If they were weighed against what you have said, they would outweigh them: 'Subhan Allah wa bihamdihi, ‘adada khalqihi, wa rida nafsihi, wa zinata ‘arshihi, wa midada (or: wa madad) kalimatihi.'"""
"505","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Seek Allah's protection from Hell, seek Allah's protection from the punishment of the grave, seek Allah's protection from the trial of the False Messiah (Dajjal), and seek Allah's protection from the trials of life and death."""
"506","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: «اللهم أصلح لي سمعي وبصري، واجعلهما الوارثين مني، وانصرني على من ظلمني وأرني منه ثأري» ""O Allah! Rectify my hearing and my sight for me, and make them my inheritors. Help me against the one who wrongs me, and show me retribution from him."""
"507","Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: «اللهم متعني بسمعي وبصري، واجعلهما الوارث مني، وانصرني على عدوي، وأرني منه ثأري» ""O Allah! Benefit me through my hearing and my sight, make them my inheritors, help me against my enemy, and show me retribution from him."""
"508","It is narrated from Tariq bin Ashyam Ashja'i that he said: We used to get up in the morning and present ourselves before the Prophet (peace be upon him); men would come, women would come. Someone would say, ""O Messenger of Allah! When I have finished my prayer, what supplication should I make?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) would say: «اللهم اغفر لي، وارحمني، واهدني، وارزقني، فقد جمعت لك دنياك وآخرتك» ""Say: O Allah! Forgive me, have mercy on me, guide me, and provide for me. These words will combine for you both the good of this world and the Hereafter."""
"509","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to come to us (i.e., to our family). One day he came and made supplication for us. Umm Sulaym (my mother) said: O Messenger of Allah! This is your humble servant Anas, will you not supplicate for him? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: «اللهم! أكثر ماله وولده، وأطل حياته، واغفر له» ""O Allah, increase his wealth and his children, lengthen his life, and forgive his sins."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated for me for three things. I have buried one hundred and three of my children, my orchard used to bear fruit twice a year, and my life became so long that I began to feel shy before people, and now I also hope for forgiveness."
"510","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The supplication of every one of you is accepted as long as he does not ask for something sinful or for breaking ties of kinship, and as long as he does not become hasty and say, 'I have made many supplications but they have not been accepted,' and then he gives up supplicating."""
"511","Amr bin Shu'aib narrates from his father, and he from his grandfather, that he said: I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: «اللهم إني أعوذ بك من الكسل والمغرم، وأعوذ بك من فتنة المسيح الدجال، وأعوذ بك من عذاب النار» ""O Allah! I seek refuge with You from laziness and debt, and I seek refuge with You from the trial of the False Messiah (Dajjal), and I seek refuge with You from the punishment of the Fire."""
"512","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it is narrated from Attar bin Abi Maimunah, who narrates from Abu Rafi’, who narrates from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek Allah’s protection from the trials of life and death, from the punishment of the grave, and from the evil of the false messiah (Dajjal)."
"513","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever does not ask Allah, Allah becomes angry with him."""
"514","It is narrated from Aban bin Uthman that I heard Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) saying that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Whoever says three times every morning and every evening: «بسم الله الذى لا يضر مع اسمه شيء فى الأرض ولا فى السماء وهو السميع العليم» , 'In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing in the earth or the sky can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, All-Knowing,' nothing will harm him."" He (Aban) had suffered paralysis on one side. The listener began to look at him, and he realized it. He said: The hadith is exactly as I have narrated to you, but on that day I did not recite this supplication so that Allah's decree could take effect."
"515","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The gates of the heavens are opened at two times, and at these times there are very few people whose supplications are not accepted: one is the time of the call to prayer (adhan), and the other is the time when ranks are formed in the way of Allah."
"516","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Shakl bin Humaid, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Please teach me a supplication from which I may benefit."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Say: «الله عافني من شر سمعي، وبصري، ولساني، وقلبي، وشر منيي» O Allah! Protect me from the evil of my hearing, my sight, my tongue, my heart, and my semen."" Waki’ said: ""Semen means adultery and immorality."""
"517","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that I heard (and in another narration it is) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate with these words: «رب (وفي الرواية الأخرى: (اللهم أعني ولا تعن علي، وانصرني ولا تنصر علي ، وامكر لي ولا تمكر علي، ويسر لي الهدى)) (وفي الأخرى : يسر الهدى إلي) ، وانصرني على من بغى علي. رب اجعلني شكاراً لك، ذكاراً لك راهباً لك، مطواعاً لك ، مخبتاً لك، أواهاً، منيباً تقبل توبتي واغسل حوبتي، وأجب دعوتي، وثبت حجتي، واهدِ قلبي، وسدد لساني، واسلل سخيمة قلبي» O my Lord! (and in another narration: O Allah!) Help me and do not help anyone against me, grant me victory and do not grant victory to anyone against me, plan for my good and do not plan against me, and make guidance easy for me, (and in another narration: make guidance easy towards me) and help me against those who oppress me. O my Lord! Make me grateful to You, one who remembers You, one who humbles himself before You, one who beseeches You for forgiveness for sins. Accept my repentance, wash away my sins, accept my supplication, establish my proof, guide my heart, make my tongue speak correctly, and remove malice from my heart."
"518","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Ka'b Qurazi, he said: Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with them both) said from the pulpit: Surely, whatever you give, no one can withhold it, and whatever Allah withholds, no one can give it, and no person of wealth can benefit you with his wealth. Whomever Allah intends good for, He grants him understanding of the religion. I heard these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) on these very planks (of the pulpit)."
"519","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, used to supplicate: «اللهم أصلح لي ديني الذى هو عصمة أمري، وأصلح لي دنياي التى فيها معاشي، واجعل الموت رحمة لي من كل سوء» ""O Allah! Set right my religion for me, for it is the safeguard of my affairs, and set right my worldly life for me, for in it is my livelihood, and make death a mercy for me from every evil."" Or as he (the Prophet) said."
"520","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek refuge from the severity of trials, from falling into wretchedness, from the evil of fate’s decrees, and from the gloating of enemies. Sufyan said: Three things are mentioned in the hadith; I have added the fourth, but I do not know which one it is."
"521","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to say: «اللهم إني أعوذ بك من العجز، والكسل، والجبن، والهرم، وأعوذ بك من فتنة المحيا والممات، وأعوذ بك من عذاب القبر» ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from helplessness, laziness, cowardice, extreme old age, and I seek refuge in You from the trials of life and death, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave."""
"522","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: «اللهم إني أعوذ بك من الهم والحزن، والعجز والكسل، والجبن والبخل وضلع الدين ، وغلبة الرجال» ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from anxiety, sorrow, incapacity, laziness, cowardice, miserliness, the burden of debt, and the overpowering of men."""
"523","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he said: Among the supplications of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, is: «اللهم اغفر لي ما قدمت وما أخرت، وما أسررت وما أعلنت، وما أنت أعلم به مني، إنك أنت المقدم والمؤخر، لا إله إلا أنت» ""O Allah! Forgive all my sins, those I committed earlier and later, those I committed secretly and openly, and those You know better than I do. You are the One Who brings forward and the One Who delays. There is no deity except You."""
"524","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah (who is Ibn Mas'ud) (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: «اللهم إني أسألك الهدى، والعفاف والغنى» ""O Allah! I ask You for guidance, chastity, and sufficiency."" And our companions have narrated from Amr: and piety."
"525","It is narrated from Thumamah bin Hazn that he said: I heard a sheikh loudly saying: «اللهم إني أعوذ بك من الشر لا يخلطه شيء» ""O Allah! I seek refuge with You from such evil in which there is nothing mixed (pure evil)."" I asked, who is this sheikh? It was said: Abu Darda."
"526","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often make this supplication: «اللهم آتنا فى الدنيا حسنة، وفي الآخرة حسنة، وقنا عذاب النار» ""O Allah! Grant us goodness in this world, goodness in the Hereafter, and save us from the punishment of Hell."" Shu’bah says that I presented this narration before ‘Ubadah, and he said that Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to make this supplication and did not narrate it as a marfu’ (directly attributed to the Prophet)."
"527","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: «اللهم إني أعوذ بك من الفقر والذلة، وأعوذ بك أن أظلم أو أُظلم » ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from poverty, from humiliation, and I seek refuge in You from doing wrong or being wronged."""
"528","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to frequently make this supplication: «اللهم! يا مقلب القلوب، ثبت قلوبنا على دينك» ""O Allah! O Turner of the hearts, keep our hearts firm upon Your religion."""
"529","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abi Awfa, who narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: «اللهم لك الحمد ملء السماوات وملء الأرض، وملء ما شئت من شيء بعد، اللهم طهرني بالبرد والثلج والماء البارد، اللهم طهرني من الذنوب ونقني كما يُنقى الثوب الأبيض من الدنس» ""O Allah! All praise is for You, as much as fills the earth, as much as fills the heavens, and as much as You will after that. O Allah! Purify me with hail, snow, and cold water. O Allah! Cleanse me from sins and purify me as a white garment is cleansed from dirt."""
"530","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that among the supplications of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was this: «اللهم إني أعوذ بك من زوال نعمتك، وتحول عافيتك، وفجأة نقمتك، وجميع سخطك» ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from the cessation of Your blessings, the change of Your well-being, the suddenness of Your punishment, and all forms of Your displeasure."""
"531","Narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw clouds rising from any direction in the sky, he would leave his work, even if it was prayer, and turn towards the cloud. If Allah drove the cloud away, he would praise Him, and if He sent down rain, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say: «اللهم صيّباً نافعاً » ""O Allah, send beneficial rain."""
"532","It is narrated from Qais that I came to Khabbab; he had seven cauterizations. He said: If it were not for the fact that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade praying for death, I would have prayed for it."
"533","Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he used to supplicate: «رب (اللهم) اغفر لي خطأي كله، وإسرافي فى أمري كله، وما أنت أعلم به مني، اللهم اغفر لي خطأي كله، وعمدي وجهلي وهزلي، وكل ذلك عندي اللهم اغفر لي ما قدمت وما أخرت، وما أسررت وما أعلنت، أنت المقدم وأنت المؤخر، وأنت على كل شيء قدير» ""O my Lord! (And in another narration: O Allah!) Forgive all my mistakes, forgive all my excesses in my affairs, and (forgive all those errors) which You know better than I do. O Allah! Forgive all my sins, those I committed deliberately, those I committed out of ignorance, those I committed in jest—all of these are from me. O Allah! Forgive me for what I did earlier and what I did later, what I did secretly and what I did openly. You are the One Who brings forward and You are the One Who delays, and You have power over all things."""
"534","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Mu’adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: “O Mu’adh!” I said: At your service. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Indeed, I love you.” I said: By Allah, I also love you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Shall I not teach you some words which you should recite after every prayer?” I said: Yes, indeed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Say! «اللهم أعني على ذكرك وشكرك ، وحسن عبادتك» .”"
"535","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: In the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man said: «الحمد لله حمداً كثيراً طيباً مباركاً فيه» ""All praise is for Allah, abundant, pure, and blessed praise."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who is the one who said this?"" The man remained silent. He thought that he had said something in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that was displeasing to him. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Who is it? He has spoken rightly."" Then the man said: ""I said it, and I only hope for good with it."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, I saw thirteen angels racing to take these words up to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."""
"536","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to enter the toilet, he would say: «اللهم إني أعوذ بك من الخبث والخبائث» ""O Allah! I seek refuge with You from male and female devils."""
"537","Narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would return from the toilet, he would say: «غفرانك» ""O Allah! I seek Your forgiveness."""
"538","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us this supplication just as he would teach us a surah from the Qur'an: «أعوذ بك من عذاب جهنم ، وأعوذ بك من عذاب القبر ، وأعوذ بك من فتنة المسيح الدجال ، وأعوذ بك من فتنة المحيا والممات ، وأعوذ بك من فتنة القبر» ."
"539","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: I spent the night at my maternal aunt Maymunah’s house. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) got up and went to relieve himself, then he washed his face and his hands, then he went back to sleep. Then he got up, came near the water-skin, opened its mouth, and performed a moderate ablution. He did not use too much water, but he performed a complete and thorough ablution. After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed. Then I also got up, stretched myself, disliking that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) might think I had been awake before. After that, I performed ablution. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was standing and praying, so I went and stood on his left side. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took hold of my ear and turned me to stand on his right side. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) completed thirteen rak‘ahs of night prayer, then he lay down and slept until he began to snore. Whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) slept, he would snore. Then Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) informed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about the prayer. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) got up and led the (morning) prayer and did not perform ablution (because it is a special characteristic of the Prophets that their ablution is not nullified by lying down). In the supplication of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) were these words: «اللهم اجعل فى قلبي نوراً ، وفي سمعي نوراً ، وعن يميني نوراً ، وعن يساري نوراً ، وفوقي نوراً ، وتحتي نوراً وأمامي نوراً وخلفي نوراً ، وأعظم لي نوراً » . Kurayb said: There were seven types of supplications in the structure, so I met a person from the descendants of Abbas, and he mentioned these seven. He said: (O Allah, place light) in my muscles, in my flesh, in my blood, in my hair, and in my skin, and he mentioned two more things."
"540","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stand for prayer in the middle of the night, he would say: «اللهم لك الحمد، أنت نور السماوات والأرض ومن فيهن، ولك الحمد، أنت قيام السماوات والأرض، ولك الحمد أنت رب السماوات والأرض ومن فيهن، أنت الحقّ، ووعدك الحقّ، ولقاؤك الحق، والجنة حق، والنار حق، والساعة حق. اللهم لك أسلمت، وبك آمنت، وعليك توكلت، وإليك أنبت، وبك خاصمت، وإليك حاكمت، فاغفر لي ما قدمت وأخرت، وأسررت وأعلنت ، أنت إلهي، لا إله إلا أنت» ""O Allah! All praise is for You alone. You are the Light of the heavens and the earth and whatever is in them. All praise is for You, for You are the Sustainer of the heavens and the earth. All praise is for You, You are the Lord of the heavens and the earth and whatever is between them. You are the Truth, Your promise is true, meeting You is true, Paradise is true, Hell is true, and the Hour is true. O Allah! I submit to You, I believe in You, I put my trust in You, I turn to You, by Your help I dispute (with the disbelievers), and I make You my judge. So forgive all my past and future, hidden and apparent sins. You alone are my deity, and there is no deity except You."""
"541","It is narrated from Rifaa Zarqi that he said: When it was the day of Uhud and the polytheists had retreated, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Straighten your rows so that I may praise my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic."" The people stood in rows behind him. He said: «اللهم لك الحمد كله، اللهم لا قابض لما بسطت، ولا مقرب لما باعدت، ولا مباعد لما قربت، ولا معطي لما منعت، ولا مانع لما أعطيت. اللهم ابسط علينا من بركاتك ورحمتك، وفضلك ورزقك، اللهم إني أسألك النعيم المقيم الذى لا يحول ولا يزول. اللهم إني أسألك النعيم يوم العيلة، والأمن يوم الحرب، اللهم عائذاً بك من سوء ما أعطيتنا، وشر ما منعت منا اللهم حبب إلينا الإيمان وزينه فى قلوبنا، وكره إلينا الكفر والفسوق والعصيان واجعلنا من الراشدين. اللهم توفنا مسلمين وأحبنا مسلمين، وألحقنا بالصالحين، غير خزايا، ولا مفتونين. اللهم قاتل الكفرة الذى يصدون عن سبيلك ويكذبون رسلك، واجعل عليهم رجزك وعذابك. اللهم قاتل الكفرة الذين أوتوا الكتاب، إله الحق» ""O Allah! All praise is for You alone. There is none who can gather what You spread, and none who can bring near what You distance, and none who can distance what You bring near. There is none who can withhold what You give, and none who can give what You withhold. O Allah! Spread upon us Your blessings, mercy, bounty, and provision. O Allah! I ask You for a lasting blessing that neither ends nor ceases. O Allah! I ask You for blessings in times of hardship and for peace on the day of battle. O Allah! I seek refuge in You from the evil of whatever You have given us and from the evil of whatever You have withheld from us. O Allah! Instill in our hearts the love of faith and beautify it in our hearts, and instill in our hearts hatred for disbelief, wickedness, and disobedience, and make us among those who are guided to goodness. O Allah! Cause us to die as Muslims, keep us alive as Muslims, and join us with the righteous. Do not disgrace us, nor let us fall into misguidance. O Allah! Kill those disbelievers who prevent others from Your path, who deny Your messengers, so send down Your punishment upon them. O True Deity! Kill those disbelievers who were given the Book."""
"542","Abdur Rahman bin Abi Bakrah says that he said to his father: O my father! I hear you recite this supplication every morning: «اللهم عافني فى بدني ، اللهم عافني فى سمعي ، اللهم عافني فى بصري ، لا إله إلا أنت» ""O Allah! Grant me well-being in my body. O Allah! Grant me well-being in my hearing. O Allah! Grant me well-being in my sight. There is no deity except You."" You recite this supplication three times in the morning and three times in the evening, and you say: «اللهم إني أعوذ بك من الكفر والفقر ، اللهم إني أعوذ بك من عذاب القبر ، لا إله إلا أنت» You recite this supplication three times in the morning and three times in the evening. He said: Yes, O my son! I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say these words, and I like to act upon his Sunnah. And he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This is the supplication of a person afflicted with anxiety: «اللهم رحمتك أرجو ، ولا تكلني إلى نفسي طرفة عين ، وأصلح لي شأني كله ، لا إله إلا أنت» O Allah! I hope for Your mercy, so do not leave me to myself even for the blink of an eye, and rectify all of my affairs. There is no deity except You."""
"543","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate at the time of distress: «لا إله إلا الله العظيم الحليم، لا إله إلا الله رب العرش العظيم، لا إله إلا الله رب السماوات ورب الأرض ورب العرش الكريم [وفي الطريق الأخرى: العظيم]، اللهم اصرف شره» “There is no deity except Allah, the Most Great, the Most Forbearing. There is no deity except Allah, the Lord of the Mighty Throne. There is no deity except Allah, the Lord of the heavens and the earth and the Lord of the Noble Throne (and in one narration: the Great). O Allah! Turn away its evil.”"
"544","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to teach us Istikhara (seeking guidance from Allah) in matters just as he would teach us a surah from the Qur'an. When any of you intends to do any work, he should pray two rak'ahs and then say: ""O Allah! I seek goodness from You by Your knowledge, and I seek power from You by Your power, and I ask You from Your great bounty, for You have power and I have no power, You know and I do not know, and You are the Knower of the unseen. O Allah! If You know that this matter is better for my religion, my livelihood, and my end, or he said: for my present or future affairs, then ordain it for me. And if You know that this matter is bad for my religion, my livelihood, and my end, or for my present or future affairs, then turn it away from me and turn me away from it, and ordain good for me wherever it may be, then make me pleased with it."" And he should mention the name of his matter."
"545","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made supplication in this mosque, ""Masjid al-Fath,"" on Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday. His supplication was accepted on Wednesday between the two prayers. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: Whenever any distressing matter befell me that would make me angry, I would seek out that very hour. I would supplicate to Allah at that hour between the two prayers on Wednesday, and I would come to know of the acceptance of the supplication. Whenever any important task or matter came before me, I would specify that time and supplicate between the two prayers on Wednesday, and I saw that the supplication was accepted."
"546","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when a man made supplication and said: «يا بديع السماوات يا حي يا قيوم! إني أسألك» ""O Originator of the heavens, O Giver of life to all, O Sustainer of all, I ask You."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know how he supplicated? By the One in Whose hand is my soul, he has called upon Allah by His Name, which, when He is called upon by it, He responds."""
"547","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), ""Tell me a supplication that I may say in my prayer."" He said: Say, «اللهم إني ظلمت نفسي ظلماً كثيراً ، ولا يغفر الذنوب إلا أنت ، فاغفر لي من عندك مغفرة ، إنك أنت الغفور الرحيم» ""I have wronged myself greatly, and none forgives sins except You, so forgive me with a complete forgiveness, for You are the Most Forgiving, Most Merciful."""
"548","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): When you are under a ruler whose harshness and oppression you fear, then say «اللهم رب السماوات السبع ورب العرش العظيم ، كن لي جاراً من فلان بن فلان وأحزابه من خلائقك؛ أن يفرط على أحد منهم ، أو يطغى ، عز جارك ، وجل ثناؤك ، ولا إله إلا أنت» ""O Allah! Lord of the seven heavens and Lord of the Mighty Throne, be my protector against so-and-so son of so-and-so from among Your creation and his group, lest any of them attack me or do injustice to me. Your protection is mighty, and Your praise is great, and there is no deity except You."""
"549","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he said: When you come to a king whose attack you fear, then say this three times: «الله أكبر . الله أعز من خلقه جميعاً ، الله أعز مما أخاف وأحذر ، أعوذ بالله الذى لا إله إلا هو ، الممسك السماوات السبع أن يقعن على الأرض إلا بإذنه؛ من شر عبدك فلان ، وجنوده وأتباعه وأشياعه من الجن والإنس . اللهم كن لي جاراً من شرهم ، جل ثناؤك ، وعز جارك ، وتبارك اسمك ، ولا إله غيرك» ""Allah is the Greatest, Allah is more powerful than all His creation. Allah is even more powerful than the one whom I fear and am afraid of. I seek refuge with Allah, besides whom there is no deity, He who holds the seven heavens so that they do not fall upon the earth except by His command, from the evil of Your such-and-such servant and his armies, and his followers, and from those among the jinn and mankind who follow him. O Allah! Be my protector against their evil, Your praise is great, Your protection is very strong, Your name is blessed, and there is no deity except You."""
"550","Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when any Muslim makes a supplication that does not involve sin or severing of family ties, then he is granted one of three things: either Allah quickly grants his supplication, or He stores it for him in the Hereafter, or He removes a similar evil from him. He (the narrator) said: ""Then we will make many supplications."" He (the Prophet) said: ""Allah is even more generous in giving."""
"551","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whenever any believer humbles his face before Allah and asks Him for anything, Allah grants it to him—either Allah gives it to him quickly in this world, or He stores it for him in the Hereafter—as long as he does not act impatiently."" They asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! What is impatience?"" He replied: ""That he says: 'I have made many supplications, many supplications, but I do not see that my prayers are being answered.'"""
"552","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""There is nothing more honorable in the sight of Allah than supplication (du'a)."""
"553","Sayyiduna Nu’man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “Supplication is worship.” Then he recited (this verse of the Qur’an): «ادعوني أستجب لكم» “Call upon Me; I will respond to you.”"
"554","Sayyiduna Ma'qil bin Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I went with Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Abu Bakr! Indeed, the shirk (polytheism) found among you is more hidden than the crawling of an ant."" Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Is shirk not that someone makes another god besides Allah? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""By the One in Whose hand is my soul, shirk is more hidden than the crawling of an ant. Shall I not tell you such words that when you say them, the minor and major (shirk) will be removed from you?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say this: «اللهم إني أعوذ بك أن أشرك بك وأنا أعلم ، وأستغفرك لما لا أعلم» ""O Allah! I seek refuge in You from associating partners with You knowingly, and I seek Your forgiveness for that which I do not know."""
"555","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: When a strong wind would blow, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would say: «اللهم إني أسألك من خير ما أُرسلت به ، وأعوذ بك من شر ما أرسلت به» ""O Allah! I ask You for the good with which it has been sent, and I seek refuge with You from the evil with which it has been sent."""
"556","Salamah (who is Ibn Akwa’) narrates that he said: When a strong wind would blow, the Prophet (ﷺ) used to say: «اللهم لاقحاً، لا عقيماً » “O Allah! Let this wind be for good and not barren.”"
"557","It is narrated from my father that he said: Do not speak ill of the wind. When you see something in it that you dislike, say: O Allah, we ask You for the good of this wind, the good of what is in it, and the good of what has been sent with it. And we seek refuge in You from the evil of this wind, the evil of what is in it, and the evil of what has been sent with it."
"558","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The wind is from the provision of Allah; it brings mercy and it brings punishment, so do not speak ill of it, but ask Allah for its good and seek refuge with Allah from its evil."""
"559","It is narrated from Musa bin Abdul Aziz, he said: Hakam narrated to me, he said: Ikrimah narrated to me that when Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) heard the sound of thunder, he used to say «سبحان الذى سبحت له» ""Glory be to Him whom you have glorified."" And he said: Thunder is an angel who drives the clouds just as a shepherd drives his goats."
"560","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) that when he used to hear the sound of thunder, he would stop speaking and say: «سبحان الذى يسبح الرعد بحمده والملائكة من خيفته» Then he would say: This is a severe warning for the inhabitants of the earth."
"561","It is narrated from Awsat bin Ismail that he said: After the death of the Prophet (peace be upon him), I heard Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) say: In the first year of Hijrah, the Prophet (peace be upon him) stood at the very place where I am standing now. Saying this, Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) began to weep, and then said: Adhere to truthfulness, for it is with righteousness, and both are in Paradise. And beware of lying, for it is with wickedness, and both are in Hell. And ask Allah for well-being, for after certainty, there is nothing better given to a person than well-being. And do not sever ties with one another, nor boycott one another, nor envy one another, nor bear malice against one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers to one another."
"562","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! Teach me a supplication by which I may ask Allah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abbas! Ask Allah for well-being."" Then he remained silent for three days. Then I came and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Teach me something by which I may ask Allah."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Abbas! O uncle of the Messenger of Allah! Ask Allah for well-being in this world and the Hereafter."""
"563","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), a man said: “O Allah! If You do not give me wealth with which I can give charity, then put me in a trial in which there is reward for me.” So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Subhan Allah, you do not have the strength for this. Why did you not say: O Allah! Grant us goodness in this world and goodness in the Hereafter and save us from the punishment of the Fire.” In another narration from him, it is reported that he said that he entered. I asked Humaid, “Did the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) enter?” He said: “Yes, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to a man who had become helpless due to illness, as if he were a chick whose feathers had been plucked. So he said to him: ‘Pray to Allah for something or ask for something.’ So the man began to say: ‘O Allah, whatever punishment You are to give me on the Day of Resurrection, give it to me in this world.’ The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ‘Subhan Allah, you do not have the strength for this,’ or he said: ‘None of you have the ability for this. Why did you not say: «اللهم آتنا فى الدنيا حسنة ، وفي الآخرة حسنة ، وقنا عذاب النار» ’ and he prayed for him, so Allah granted him healing.”"
"564","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: A man says: O Allah! I seek refuge in You from the hardship of trials, then he becomes silent. After saying this, he should then say: Except for such a trial in which there is elevation of ranks."
"565","It is narrated from Abu Nofal bin Abi Aqrab that his father asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about fasting. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fast one day in every month."" I said, ""May my parents be sacrificed for you, please allow me more."" He said: ""What is this, wanting to do more, wanting to do more? Fast two days in every month."" I said, ""May my parents be sacrificed for you, I find myself stronger than that."" He said: ""Stronger, stronger!"" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent, until I thought that he would never allow more than that. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Alright, fast three days in every month."""
"566","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) when a very foul-smelling wind began to blow and it became intense. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do you know what this is? This is the stench of those who backbite the believers."" In another narration, it is stated that some hypocrites backbit some Muslims, and this wind was sent because of that."
"567","It is narrated from Ibn Umm Abd, that is, Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): Whoever defends a believer in whose presence he is being backbitten, Allah will grant him a better reward in this world and the Hereafter. Whoever does not defend a believer in whose presence he is being backbitten, Allah will give him an evil recompense in this world and the Hereafter. And no one has eaten a worse morsel than the one who backbites a believing man; if what he says is actually found in him, then he has committed backbiting, and if he says something he does not know, then he has slandered him."
"568","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came to two graves, the occupants of which were being punished. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""They are not being punished for something major. And why not? One of them used to backbite people, and the other did not take care to protect himself from urine (splashes)."" Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a fresh date-palm branch or two branches, then he broke them and ordered that a branch be planted on each grave. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Listen! Their punishment will be lightened as long as these remain fresh,"" or he said: ""until they dry out."""
"569","It is narrated from Qais that Sayyiduna Amr bin Al-Aas (may Allah be pleased with him) was traveling with a group of his companions. They passed by a dead mule that had become bloated. He said: By Allah! If any one of you were to fill his stomach by eating this, it would be better for him than eating the flesh of his Muslim brother."
"570","570/738 From ‘Ubada ibn al-Walid ibn al-Samit who said: I went out with my father while I was a young boy, and we met an old man [ عليه بردة ومعافري، وعلى غلامه بردة ومعافري] . I said: “O uncle, what prevented you from giving your boy this striped garment, and taking the cloak, so you would have two cloaks, and he would have the striped garment?” He turned to my father and said: “Is this your son?” He said: “Yes.” He then wiped my head and said: “May Allah bless you. I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: ‘Feed them from what you eat, and clothe them from what you wear.’ O son of my brother, the loss of worldly goods is more beloved to me than that he should take from the goods of the Hereafter.” I said: “O my father! Who is this man?” He said: “Abu al-Yusr [كعب] ibn ‘Amr.”"
"571","Muhammad bin Ziyad narrates that I witnessed the era of the Salaf (the Companions). These people used to live in the same house with their families. Often it would happen that a guest would come to someone, and another person’s pot would be on the fire. The one who had the guest would take that pot for his guest. The owner of the pot, not finding his pot, would ask, “Who has taken the pot?” The one with the guest would say, “We have taken it for the guest.” The owner of the pot would say, “May Allah bless you in it,” or would say something similar. Baqiyyah said: Muhammad used to say: The same would happen with bread baking. And there would only be wooden walls between the two households. Baqiyyah says: I also witnessed this, meaning I found Muhammad bin Ziyad and his companions in this state."
"572","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a man came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked his noble wives, and all of them replied that they had nothing except water. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Who will take this guest, or who will host him?"" One man from among the Ansar said, ""I will."" He took him to his wife and said to her, ""Honor the guest of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)."" She said, ""We have nothing except the food for the children."" He said, ""Prepare the food, and adjust the lamp. Put the children to sleep when they ask for dinner."" The wife prepared the food, adjusted the lamp, and put the children to sleep. Then she got up as if she was fixing the lamp, but she turned it off, and made the guest feel as if both of them (husband and wife) were eating as well, though they both spent the night hungry. In the morning, he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him), upon seeing him, said: ""Allah smiled at, or was pleased with, your action last night."" Upon this, Allah revealed this verse: «ويؤثرون على أنفسهم ولو كان بهم خصاصة ومن يوق شح نفسه فأولئك هم المفلحون»"
"573","It is narrated from Abu Shurayh Adawi that he said: My two ears heard and my eyes saw when the Prophet (peace be upon him) was saying: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should honor his guest by giving him a gift. Someone asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is meant by his gift? He said: ""A day and a night. Recommended hospitality is for three days, and whatever is beyond that is charity for the guest. It is not permissible for him to stay with him to the extent that he puts him in difficulty. Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day should speak good or remain silent."""
"574","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Hospitality is for three days, and whatever is beyond that will be charity."""
"575","Abu Karima Shami narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""Hospitality for one night is obligatory upon every Muslim. Whoever spends the night in someone’s courtyard, it becomes a debt upon him; if he wishes, he may demand repayment of the debt, and if he wishes, he may forgo it."""
"576","Sayyiduna Uqbah bin Amir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), ""O Messenger of Allah! You send us (for jihad), and we camp near a people, but they do not host us. What do you think about this?"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to us: ""If you camp near a people and an order is issued for you for what is due to a guest, then accept it. If they do not do so, then take from them the right of the guest which was permissible for them."" (When you go to a people, I will tell you what a guest should do. Draw their attention. If they do not show hospitality, then take as much as is due to a guest.)"
"577","It is narrated from Sahl bin Sa’d that Abu Usaid Sa’idi (may Allah be pleased with him) invited the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to his wedding, and his wife herself was serving the people that day, and she was the bride. So she (the wife) said, or he (the husband) said: Do you know what I had soaked and prepared as nabidh for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I had soaked some dates in a plate overnight."
"578","Nuaim bin Qanab narrates that I came to Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) but did not find him. I asked his wife: Where is Abu Dharr? She said: He has gone to do some work, he will be back soon. I sat down to wait for him. When Abu Dharr came, he had two camels with him, tied one behind the other. Each of them had a small water skin tied around its neck. He unloaded them and then came to me. I said: Abu Dharr! There is no one whose meeting I like more than yours, and no one whose meeting I dislike more than yours. He said: May Allah bless your father, how did these two things come together? I said: In the time of ignorance, I buried a girl alive. I was afraid that if I met you, you might say that now there is no repentance or salvation for you, and I also hoped that you might say that there is repentance and salvation is possible. He said: Did you commit this sin in the time of ignorance? I said: Yes. He said: Allah has forgiven all past sins. After that, he said to his wife: Bring food for us. She refused. He asked again, she refused again, until both their voices were raised. Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Listen, you cannot go beyond the limit that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has set regarding you. I said: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say about her? He said: Woman was created from a rib, and if you try to straighten her, you will break her, and if you deal with her kindly, there will remain some crookedness, but you will be able to get along. Then she got up and brought tharid (a dish of meat and bread), as if it was a wild pigeon (because tharid contains both meat and bread). (Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him) said: Eat, I will not frighten you (the food seemed little, and if Abu Dharr ate, perhaps the guest would remain hungry), because I am fasting. Then he got up and started praying, and he prayed a light prayer. Then he came and started eating. I said: Alas, I did not expect that you would lie to me. He said: May Allah bless your father, since you met me, I have not lied. I said: Did you not tell me that you are fasting? He said: Why not. I have fasted three days of this month, and the reward (of the whole month) has been written for me, and food is lawful for me (meaning it is a voluntary fast, I can break it because I have already received the reward of fasting for the whole month)."
"579","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “The best dinar is the one a man spends on his dependents. After that, it is the one he spends on his friends in the way of Allah, then the one he spends on his animal in the way of Allah.” Abu Qilabah says that he (the Prophet) started with dependents—how could there be a greater reward than for the one who spends on his small children until Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, makes him independent of them?"
"580","Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud Badri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “Whoever spends on his family and intends reward for it, it becomes charity for him.”"
"581","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): A man said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I have one dinar."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Spend it on yourself."" He said, ""I have another one."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Spend it on your servant,"" or he said, ""Spend it on your children."" He said, ""I have another one."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Spend it in the way of Allah, and this is the lowest of the ranks."""
"582","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that he narrates from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""There are four types of dinar: one dinar is that which you give to a poor person, one is that which you spend in freeing a slave, one is that which you spend in jihad, and one is that which you spend on your family. The most virtuous dinar is the one which you spend on your family."""
"583","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) that he informed them that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sa’d: “You will be rewarded for every expenditure by which you seek the pleasure of Allah, even for that which you put in your wife’s mouth.”"
"584","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Our Lord, Blessed and Exalted, descends to the lowest heaven every night when one third of the night remains, and says: Who is there who supplicates to Me so that I may answer his supplication? Who is there who asks of Me so that I may give to him? Who is there who seeks forgiveness from Me so that I may forgive him?"""
"585","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that Sayyida Sawda (may Allah be pleased with her) sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to travel at night during the night of Muzdalifah, as she was a woman of heavy build and slow pace, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted her permission."
"586","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) distributed the spoils of the Battle of Hunayn at the place of Ji'ranah, people crowded around him. Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah sent one of His servants to a people, but they denied him and wounded him. So he kept wiping the blood from his forehead and kept saying: 'O Allah! Forgive my people, for they do not know.'"" Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says: It is as if I am seeing the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) describing a person who is wiping his forehead."
"587","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When you hear someone saying that the people are ruined, then he is the most ruined among them."""
"588","Sayyiduna Buraidah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not call a hypocrite a leader. If he becomes your leader, then you have angered your Lord, Allah the Mighty and Majestic."""
"589","Adi bin Artah narrates that when any man among the companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) was considered chaste, he would say: O Allah! Do not hold me accountable for what these people say (about me), and forgive me for (my shortcomings) which they do not know."
"590","It is narrated from Abu Qilabah that Abu Abdullah said to Abu Mas'ud, or Abu Mas'ud said to Abu Abdullah: What have you heard from the Prophet (peace be upon him) about «زعم» ? He said: «زعم» is a bad mount for a person (that is, it is a lie)."
"591","Abu Mas'ud said: And I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say: Cursing a believer is like killing him."
"592","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that none of you should say about something he does not know that ""Allah knows,"" while what Allah knows is something else. Thus, he is including in Allah's knowledge something he does not know. This is a great sin in the sight of Allah. (That is, if someone says, ""Allah knows, the truth is such,"" while in reality the truth is not such, then he is attributing to Allah's knowledge something which is not true in reality, so it should not be attributed to Allah.)"
"593","It is narrated from Abu Tufail that Ibn al-Kawwa asked Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) about the Milky Way: He said, ""It is a valley in the sky; from there the sky is opened with extremely abundant rainwater."""
"594","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them): The rainbow is a protection (safeguard) for the people of the earth from drowning, and the Milky Way is the gate of the sky from where it emerges."
"595","It is narrated from Abu Harith Kermani that he said: I heard a man saying to Abu Raja: I greet you with peace and I pray to Allah that He admits me and you into the place of His mercy. He (Abu Raja) said: Does anyone have the power to do that? He asked: What do you mean by the place of mercy? He said: Paradise. He (Abu Raja) said: You have not said correctly. That man asked Abu Raja: What is the place of mercy according to you? I said: It is the Lord of the worlds."
"596","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""None of you should say, 'O misfortune of time.' Verily, Allah is the One who manages time (the system of time)."" And in another narration: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: ""I am time; I send the night and the day, then when I will, I will withhold them."" And do not ever call grapes 'Karam,' for 'Karam' is a Muslim man."
"597","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a she-camel which was to be slaughtered in Makkah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ride on it."" He said: ""It is a she-camel to be slaughtered in Makkah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ride on it."" He said: ""It is a she-camel to be slaughtered in Makkah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Ride on it."" He said: ""But it is a she-camel to be slaughtered in Makkah."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Woe to you, ride on it."""
"598","It is narrated from Miswar bin Rifa’ah Qarzi that he heard Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) being asked a question by a man. The man was saying: I have eaten bread and meat. Should I perform ablution? He (Ibn Abbas) said: Woe to you, will you perform ablution after eating pure and clean food?"
"599","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that on the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was at the place of Ji‘ranah (the name of a place seven miles from Makkah towards Ta’if). Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) had a piece of gold in his lap, and he was distributing it. A man came to you and said: “Be just. You are not being just.” You (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Woe to you! If I do not act justly, then who will act justly?” Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to strike the neck of this hypocrite.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “He is with his companions.” Or he said: “He is among his companions. These people will recite the Qur’an, but the Qur’an will not go below their throats. They will go out of the religion just as an arrow passes out of the bow.” I said to Sufyan: “Did Qurrat narrate this from ‘Amr and ‘Amr from Jabir?” He said: “I do not remember it being from ‘Amr, this hadith was narrated to us by Abu Zubair from Jabir.”"
"600","It is narrated from Bashir bin Ma’bad Sudusi, whose name was Zahm bin Ma’bad. He migrated and presented himself to the service of the Prophet (ﷺ). The Prophet (ﷺ) asked, “What is your name?” He replied, “Zahm.” The Prophet (ﷺ) said, “No, rather you are Bashir.” He narrates that once I was walking with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). The Prophet (ﷺ) said, “O son of Khasasiyyah (she was his grandmother or maternal grandmother)! What is the matter that you have started to be displeased with Allah, while your condition is that you are walking with the Messenger of Allah?” I said, “May my parents be sacrificed for you, I am not displeased with Allah over anything. I have attained every kind of good.” While the Prophet (ﷺ) was passing by some graves—and in one narration, he passed by the graves of the polytheists—the Prophet (ﷺ) said, “These people have gone ahead, leaving behind much goodness.” The Prophet (ﷺ) said this three times. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) passed by some other graves—and in one narration, he came to the graves of the Muslims—and said three times, “These people have attained much goodness.” Then the gaze of the Prophet (ﷺ) was raised and he saw a man walking among the graves wearing shoes. The Prophet (ﷺ) said, “O wearer of leather shoes! Remove your leather shoes.” So the man looked, and when he saw the Prophet (ﷺ), he took off his shoes and threw them away."
"601","601/776 From Muhammad ibn Hilal: He saw the chambers of the wives of the Prophet, peace be upon him, made of palm branches covered with haircloths(1). So I asked him about the house of Aisha. He said: Its door was facing the direction of al-Sham. I said: Was it a single leaf or double-leafed? He said: It was a single door. I said: Of what was it made? He said: Of juniper or teak."
"602","602/778 From Abu Huraira: A man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah! Which charity has the greatest reward? He said: ""By your father, I will surely inform you: To give charity while you are healthy and stingy, fearing poverty and hoping for wealth, and not to delay until when the soul reaches the throat, you say: For so-and-so is such-and-such, and for so-and-so is such-and-such, and it has already belonged to so-and-so."""
"603","603/779 From Abdullah [ هو ابن مسعود] who said: ""If one of you seeks a need, let him seek it gently; for he will only have what has been decreed for him. And let none of you come to his companion and praise him, for he will break his back."""
"604","604/780 From Abu Azza; Yasar ibn Abdullah al-Hudhali, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Indeed, when Allah intends to take the soul of a servant in a land, He makes for him in it – or: within it – a need."""
"605","605/783-(Sahih) From Ibn Abbas: A man said to the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""Whatever Allah wills and you will!"" He said: ""Have you made me a rival to Allah?! Whatever Allah alone wills."""
"606","606/784- (Hasan al-Isnad) From Abdullah ibn Dinar who said: I went out with Abdullah ibn Umar to the market, and he passed by a young girl singing, so he said: ""If Satan were to leave anyone alone, he would have left this one."" 607/786- (Sahih al-Isnad) From Ibn Abbas: ""? And of mankind is he who purchases idle talk ? [لقمان: 6] "", he said: ""Singing and its likes."""
"607","From Ibn Abbas: {‏ وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ يَشْتَرِي لَهْوَ الْحَدِيثِ ‏} , (Luqman: 6), he said: Singing and its likes."
"608","608/787-(Hasan) from Al-Bara’ ibn ‘Azib who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Spread peace and you will be safe, and al-ashrah is evil.” Abu Mu’awiyah said: Al-ashrah means frivolity."
"609","609/789- (Hasan) From Ibn Mas'ud who said: ""You are in a time when its jurists are many, its preachers are few, its questioners are few, and its givers are many; in it, action leads desire. And there will come after you a time when its jurists are few, its preachers are many, its questioners are many, and its givers are few; in it, desire leads action. Know that good guidance—in the end of times—is better than some deeds.""(1)."
"610","610/790- (Sahih) From al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Tufayl who said: I said to [ لَهُ ] : Did you see the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him? He said: ""Yes, and I do not know of any man alive on the face of the earth who saw the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, other than myself."" He said: ""And he was white, handsome of face."""
"611","611/791-(Hasan) From Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Righteous guidance, good demeanor, and moderation are a part of twenty-five parts of prophethood."""
"612","612/792-(Sahih) From Ikrimah: I asked Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: Did you ever hear the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, recite poetry? She said: Sometimes, when he entered his house, he would say: ""And news will be brought to you by one whom you did not supply.""(1)."
"613","613/793-(Sahih li-ghayrih) from Ibn Abbas who said: It is a saying of a prophet: ""And news will be brought to you by one whom you did not supply provisions."""
"614","614/795-(Sahih) From Alqama bin Wa'il, [عن أبيه] from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""None of you should say: 'al-Karam', but say: 'al-Habalah'"" (1) meaning: the grape."
"615","615/796-(Sahih) From Abu Huraira: The Prophet, peace be upon him, passed by a man who was leading a sacrificial camel, so he said: ""Ride it."" The man said: O Messenger of Allah! It is a sacrificial camel. He said: ""Ride it."" He said: It is a sacrificial camel! He said on the third or fourth time: ""Woe to you, ride it."""
"616","616/789-(Authentic chain) From Habib ibn Subhan al-Asadi: ""I saw Ammar perform the obligatory prayer, then he said to a man next to him: 'O so-and-so!' Then he stood up."""
"617","617/799-(Sahih) From al-Sharid who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, mounted me behind him and said: ""Do you have any poetry of Umayyah ibn Abi al-Salt?"" I said yes; so I recited to him a verse, and he said: ""Go on [هيه/869] ""(2) until I had recited one hundred verses to him, [فقال: ""إن كاد ليسلم""] ."
"618","618/800- (Sahih) From Aisha who said: Do not abandon the night prayer; for the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, ""would not leave it, and if he was ill or lazy, he would pray sitting."""
"619","619/801- (Sahih) From Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to frequently say: ""O Allah, I seek refuge in You from worry and grief, from incapacity and laziness, from cowardice and miserliness, from the burden of debt, and from being overpowered by men."""
"620","620/803- (Sahih) From Abu Dharr [قال] : The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, went toward al-Baqi', and I went following him. He turned and saw me. He said: ""O Abu Dharr!"" I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and your happiness, and I am your ransom. He said: ""Indeed, those who have much are the ones who will have little on the Day of Resurrection, except for those who say like this and like this in right."" I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: ""Like this"" (three times), then Uhud appeared to us and he said: ""O Abu Dharr!"" I said: At your service, O Messenger of Allah, and your happiness, and I am your ransom. He said: ""It would not please me that Uhud should be gold for the family of Muhammad, and that a dinar—or he said: a mithqal—should remain with them by evening."" Then a valley appeared to us, so he hastened, and I thought he had a need, so I sat on the edge, and he delayed for me. I became concerned for him, then I heard him as if he was conversing with a man, then he came out to me alone. I said: O Messenger of Allah! Who was the man you were conversing with? He said: ""Did you hear him?"" I said: Yes. He said: ""It was Jibril who came to me and gave me glad tidings that whoever from my ummah dies not associating anything with Allah will enter Paradise."" I said(5): Even if he committed adultery and theft? He said: Yes."
"621","621/804-(Sahih) From Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I never saw the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, ransom a man after Sa'd. I heard him say: ""Shoot, may my father and mother be ransomed for you."""
"622","622/805-(Sahih) From Buraidah: The Prophet, peace be upon him, went out to the mosque—and Abu Musa was reciting—so he said: ""Who is this?"" I said: ""It is I, Buraidah, may I be ransomed for you."" He said: ""This one has been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dawud."""
"623","623/807- (Authentic by other than itself) From Anas who said: I was a servant of the Prophet, peace be upon him. He said: I used to enter without asking permission, so one day I came, and he said: ""Stay as you are, my son; for something has happened after you: do not enter except with permission."""
"624","624/808- (Authentic chain, Mawquf) From Abu Sa'sa'ah, that Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said to him: ""O my son!"""
"625","625/809-(Sahih) From Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""None of you should say: 'My soul has become filthy,' but let him say: 'My soul has become uneasy.'"""
"626","626/810- (Sahih) From Sahl ibn Hunayf, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""Let none of you say: 'My soul has become filthy,' but let him say: 'My soul has become weary.'"" (1)(2)."
"627","627/811-(Sahih) From Shurayh ibn Hani who said: Hani ibn Yazid told me that when he came as a delegate to the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, with his people, the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, heard them calling him Abu al-Hakam. So the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, called him and said: ""Indeed, Allah is al-Hakam, and to Him belongs the judgment. So why are you called Abu al-Hakam?"" He said: No, but my people, when they differ about something, they come to me and I judge between them, and both parties are pleased. He said: ""How excellent this is!"" Then he said: ""What children do you have?"" I said: I have Shurayh, Abdullah, and Muslim; the sons of Hani. He said: ""Who is the eldest of them?"" I said: Shurayh. He said: ""Then you are Abu Shurayh,"" and he prayed for him and his children. And the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, heard [ قوماً ] (1) them calling a man among them: Abd al-Hajar, so the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, said: ""What is your name?"" He said: Abd al-Hajar. He said: ""No. You are Abdullah."" Shurayh said: And when Hani was about to return to his land, he came to the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, and said: Tell me something that makes Paradise obligatory. He said: ""You must have good speech and offer food."""
"628","628/813-(Authentic by other than itself, without the reason for the hadith and the haste) From Ibn Abbas who said: The Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came quickly while we were sitting, and his haste towards us startled us. When he reached us, he greeted us with salam, then said: ""I came to you quickly to inform you about Laylat al-Qadr, but I forgot it between me and you. So seek it in the last ten nights."""
"629","629/814 (Authentic except for the phrase ""the prophets"") - From Abu Wahb [الجشمي] – and he had companionship – from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""Name yourselves with the names of the prophets. The most beloved names to Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, are: Abdullah and Abdur-Rahman. The truest of them are Harith and Hammam, and the ugliest of them are: Harb: Harb, and Murrah."""
"630","630/815-(Sahih) From Jabir who said: A boy was born to a man among us and he named him al-Qasim. We said: ""We will give you the kunya Abu al-Qasim, and no honor (for that)."" The Prophet, peace be upon him, was informed, and he said: ""Name your son Abd al-Rahman."""
"631","631/816- From Sahl who said: Al-Mundhir ibn Abi Usayd was brought to the Prophet, peace be upon him, when he was born, and he placed him on his thigh—and Abu Usayd was sitting. The Prophet, peace be upon him, was distracted by something in front of him, and Abu Usayd ordered his son to be taken from the thigh of the Prophet, peace be upon him. When the Prophet, peace be upon him, regained awareness, he said: ""Where is the boy?"" Abu Usayd said: ""We took him away, O Messenger of Allah!"" He said: ""What is his name?"" He said: ""So-and-so."" He said: ""No, rather his name is Al-Mundhir,"" so he named him that day Al-Mundhir."
"632","632/817-(Sahih) From Abu Huraira who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The most despicable name in the sight of Allah is a man who calls himself King of Kings."""
"633","633/818- (Authentic due to other chains) From Talq ibn Habib who said: I was among the people who most strongly denied intercession(1), so I asked Jabir, and he said: O Taliq, I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: ""They will come out of the Fire after entering it,"" and we recite what you recite."
"634","634/820- (Sahih) From Ibn Umar; that the Prophet, peace be upon him, changed the name of 'Asiya, and said: ""You are Jamila."""
"635","635/821- (Sahih) From Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata; that he entered upon Zaynab bint Abi Salama, and she asked him about the name of a sister of his with him? [قال] : So I said: Her name is Barra. She said: Change her name; for the Prophet, peace be upon him, married Zaynab bint Jahsh and her name was Barra, so he changed her name to Zaynab. He entered upon Umm Salama when he married her, and my name was Barra, and he heard her calling me: Barra, so he said: ""Do not ascribe purity to yourselves; for Allah is most knowing of the righteous among you and the wicked. Name her: Zaynab."" So she said: Thus she is Zaynab. So I said to her: Name (her)?(1)"
"636","636/825- (Hasan) From Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: A man called Shihab was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Rather, you are Hisham."""
"637","637/826-(Sahih) From Muti’ who said: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say on the day of the conquest of Mecca: ""No Qurayshi shall be killed in captivity after today until the Day of Resurrection."" None of the disobedient ones of Quraysh attained Islam except Muti’; his name was Al-‘As, so the Prophet, peace be upon him, named him: Muti’."
"638","638/827- (Sahih) From Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""O Aish! This is Jibril [وهو/1036] who sends you greetings of peace."" She said: [فقلت: ] And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah [وبركاته] (1). She said: And he sees what I do not see. And in another narration: You see what I do not see, meaning by that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him."
"639","639/830- (Sahih) From Layla; the wife of Bashir narrates, from Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyyah. And his name was Zahm. The Prophet, peace be upon him, named him Bashir."
"640","640/831- (Sahih) From Ibn Abbas: The name of Juwayriya was Barra, so the Prophet, peace be upon him, named her Juwayriya."
"641","641/833- (Sahih) From Jabir, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""If I live, I will forbid my ummah—if Allah wills—that any of them name (their children) Barakah, Nafi‘, or Aflah, (and I do not know if he said: 'Rafi‘' or not?) It would be said: Is Barakah here? And it would be said: He is not here."" Then the Prophet, peace be upon him, passed away and did not forbid that."
"642","642/834 (Sahih) And from him through another route: The Prophet, peace be upon him, intended to forbid naming with Ya'la, Baraka, Nafi', Yasar, Aflah, and the like, then he remained silent about it afterward and did not say anything."
"643","643/835 (Hasan) From Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, withdrew from his wives, I saw Rabah, the servant of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, so I called out: O Rabah! Seek permission for me to enter upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him."
"644","644/836 (Sahih) From Abu Huraira, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya; for I am Abu al-Qasim."""
"645","645/837 (Sahih) From Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, was in the market, and a man said: O Abu al-Qasim! So the Prophet, peace be upon him, turned to him. The man said: O Messenger of Allah! I was only calling this one. So the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya."""
"646","646/838 (Sahih) From Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam who said: ""The Prophet, peace be upon him, named me Yusuf, seated me on his lap, and wiped his hand over my head.""(2)."
"647","647/839 (Sahih) From Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: A man from among us, the Ansar, had a boy born to him, and he wanted to name him Muhammad. (In one narration here: The Ansari said: I carried him on my neck and brought him to the Prophet, peace be upon him.) (In another: A boy was born to him, and they wanted to name him Muhammad.) He said: ""Name yourselves with my name, but do not use my kunya; for I have been made (in another narration: I have been sent as) a distributor, dividing among you."""
"648","648/840 (Sahih) From Abu Musa who said: ""A boy was born to me, so I brought him to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he named him Ibrahim! He chewed a date and put it in his mouth, supplicated for blessing for him, and handed him back to me."" And he was the eldest child of Abu Musa."
"649","649/841 (Sahih) From Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from his father, from his grandfather, that he came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: ""What is your name?"" He said: Huzn. He said: ""You are Sahl."" He said: I will not change a name my father gave me! Ibn al-Musayyib said: So harshness remained among us after that. (And from another route from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib that his grandfather was Huzn ... and he mentioned it as mursal.)"
"650","650/842 (Sahih) From Jabir who said: A man among us had a boy born to him, so he named him al-Qasim. The Ansar said: ""We will not give you the kunya Abu al-Qasim, nor will we let you be delighted."" So he went to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and told him what [الأنصار] had said. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""The Ansar have done well; name yourselves with my name, but do not take my kunya, for I am al-Qasim."""
"651","651/843 (Sahih) From Ibn al-Hanafiyyah who said: It was a concession for Ali, he said: O Messenger of Allah! If a child is born to me after you, may I name him with your name and give him your kunya? He said: ""Yes."""
"652","652/844 From Abu Huraira, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade us from combining his name and his kunyah, and he said: ""I am Abu al-Qasim, Allah gives, and I distribute."""
"653","653/846 From Usama ibn Zayd: ""The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came upon a gathering in which was Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul, and that was before Abdullah ibn Ubayy had accepted Islam. He said: 'Do not harm us in our gathering!' Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, entered upon Sa'd ibn Ubadah and said: 'O Sa'd! Do you not hear what Abu Hubab says?!'—meaning Abdullah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul(1)."""
"654","654/847 Narrated Anas: The Prophet, peace be upon him, used to come to us—and I had a little brother who was nicknamed Abu Umair, and he had a small bird he used to play with, but it died. The Prophet, peace be upon him, entered and saw him sad. He said: ""What is the matter with him?"" It was said to him: His little bird has died. He said: ""O Abu Umair! What happened to the little bird?"" (1)."
"655","655/848 From Ibrahim [هو النخغي] : ""That Abdullah gave Alqama the kunya: Abu Shibl(1), though no child had been born to him."""
"656","656/849 From Alqama [ هو ابن وائل] who said: ""Abdullah gave me a kunya before I had a child born to me."""
"657","657/851 From Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: O Prophet of Allah! Will you not give me a kunya(1)? He said: ""Take a kunya by your son,"" meaning Abdullah ibn al-Zubair, so she was called: Umm Abdullah."
"658","658/852 From Sahl ibn Sa'd: The most beloved of names to Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was Abu Turab, and he used to rejoice when he was called by it. No one named him ""Abu Turab"" except the Prophet, peace be upon him; he (Ali) had made Fatima angry, so he went out and lay down by the wall in the mosque. The Prophet, peace be upon him, came looking for him and was told: ""He is lying by the wall."" The Prophet, peace be upon him, came to him and found that his back was covered with dust, so the Prophet, peace be upon him, began to wipe the dust off his back and said: ""Sit up, Abu Turab!"""
"659","659/853 From Anas who said: While the Prophet, peace be upon him, was in some of our palm groves—a grove belonging to Abu Talha—he went out to relieve himself, and Bilal was walking [وراءه، يكرم النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم أن يمشي] (1) beside him. The Prophet, peace be upon him, passed by a grave and stood, until Bilal caught up with him. He said: ""Woe to you, O Bilal! Do you hear what I hear?"" He said: ""I do not hear anything."" He said: ""The occupant of this grave is being punished."" And they found a Jew(3)."
"660","660/854 From Qais [ وهو ابن أبي حازم ] who said: I heard Muawiya say to his younger brother, ""Let the boy ride behind you,"" but he refused. So Muawiya said to him, ""What a bad way you have been taught."" Qais said: Then I heard Abu Sufyan say, ""Leave your brother alone."""
"661","661/855 From Amr ibn al-As: ""If companions become many, creditors become many."" I said to Musa: And what are creditors? He said: Rights."
"662","662/857 From Mutarrif who said: I accompanied Imran ibn Husayn from Kufa to Basra, and there was hardly a place where he stayed except that he would recite poetry to me, and he said: ""Indeed, in ambiguous speech there is an alternative to lying."""
"663","663/858 From Ubayy ibn Ka'b; that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Indeed, among poetry there is wisdom."""
"664","664/859 From Al-Aswad ibn Sari’, [ قال: كنت شاعراً، فأتيت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم فـ/861] I said: O Messenger of Allah! I have praised my Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, with words of praise. He said: ""Indeed, your Lord loves praise,"" and he did not add anything to that."
"665","665/860 From Abu Huraira who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""For a man's belly to be filled with pus [حتى] (1) that harms him (2), is better than for it to be filled with poetry."""
"666","666/862 From Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Hassan ibn Thabit sought permission from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, to satirize the polytheists. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""But what about my lineage?"" He said: ""I will extract you from them as a hair is extracted from dough."""
"667","667/863 From Urwah who said: I went to insult Hassan in the presence of Aisha, and she said: Do not insult him; for he ""used to defend (3) the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him."""
"668","668/865 From Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Poetry is like speech; its good is like good speech, and its bad is like bad speech."""
"669","669/866 From Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her; she used to say: ""Poetry, some of it is good and some of it is bad. Take what is good and leave what is bad. Indeed, I have memorized from the poetry of Ka'b ibn Malik poems, among them a poem containing forty verses, and less than that."""
"670","670/867 From Shurayh who said: I said to Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, ever recite any poetry? She said: He used to recite some lines of poetry by Abdullah ibn Rawaha: ""And news will be brought to you by one whom you did not supply.""(1)."
"671","671/870 From Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""For one of you to have his belly filled with pus is better for him than to have it filled with poetry."""
"672","672/871 From Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: ""And the poets are followed by the deviators"" [الشعراء: 224] up to His saying: ""And that they say what they do not do"" [الشعراء: 226] . So that was abrogated and an exception was made, and He said: ""Except those who believe"" up to His saying: ""they return"" (1)."
"673","673/872 From Ibn Abbas: That a man – or a Bedouin – came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and spoke with clear speech, so the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Indeed, some eloquence is magic, and indeed, some poetry is wisdom."""
"674","674/874 From Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""The greatest of people in sin is a poet who satirizes an entire tribe, and a man who denies his father."""
"675","675/875 From Ibn Umar who said: Two men from the east came as preachers during the time of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him. They stood up and spoke, then sat down. Then Thabit ibn Qays, the preacher of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, stood up and spoke, and the people were amazed at their speech. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, then stood up to preach and said: ""O people! Say what you have to say, for indeed splitting hairs in speech is from the Shaytan."" Then the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Indeed, some eloquence is magic."""
"676","676/876 From Anas who said: A man delivered a sermon before Umar and spoke at length, so Umar said: ""Indeed, excessive speech in sermons is among the rants of Satan.""(3)."
"677","677/877- From Abu Yazid – or: Ma'n ibn Yazid – that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Gather in your mosques, and whenever a group gathers, let them inform me."" The first to come to us arrived, sat down, and one of us spoke, then said: ""Praise be to Allah, for whom there is no destination for praise except Him, nor any outlet beyond Him."" He became angry and stood up, so we blamed each other among ourselves and said: ""The first to come to us has left; he went to another mosque and sat there."" So we went to him, spoke to him, and he came with us and sat in his seat or near his seat. Then he said: ""Praise be to Allah, who places whatever He wills before Him, and whatever He wills behind Him. Indeed, among eloquence there is magic."" Then he commanded us and taught us."
"678","678/878- From Aisha: The Prophet, peace be upon him, was unable to sleep one night, so he said: ""If only a righteous man from my companions would come to guard me tonight."" Then we heard the sound of weapons, so he said: ""Who is this?"" He said: Sa'd, O Messenger of Allah! I have come to guard you. So the Prophet, peace be upon him, slept until we heard his snoring."
"679","679/879 From Anas ibn Malik who said: There was a panic in Medina, so the Prophet, peace be upon him, borrowed a horse belonging to Abu Talha — called Al-Mandub — and rode it. When he returned, he said: ""We saw nothing (to fear), and indeed we found it (the horse) to be like a sea."""
"680","680/880 From Nafi‘ who said: ""Ibn Umar used to strike his son for grammatical mistakes."""
"681","681/882 From Aisha, the wife of the Prophet, peace be upon him: Some people asked the Prophet, peace be upon him, about the soothsayers. He said to them: ""They are nothing."" They said: O Messenger of Allah! But they sometimes tell of something that comes true? The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""That is a word [من الحق] (1) snatched by a devil, who cackles it into the ear of his friend like the cackling of a hen, and they mix with it more than a hundred lies."""
"682","682/883 From Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was on a journey, and the camel driver began to chant. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Be gentle, O Anjasha—woe to you—with the glass vessels."""
"683","683/884 From Umar (as I see it, Abu [the narrator] doubted) (1) that he said: ""It is enough falsehood for a person to narrate everything he hears."""
"684","684/884m- He said: And as I see, he said: Umar said: ""Is there not in equivocation what suffices a Muslim [من] (2) from lying?"""
"685","685/886 From Amr ibn al-As who said: ""I am amazed at the man who flees from destiny, while he is meeting it! And he sees the speck in his brother's eye, and leaves the log in his own eye! And he brings out the malice from his brother's soul, and leaves the malice in his own soul! And I have never entrusted my secret to anyone and then blamed him for disclosing it, and how can I blame him when I myself could not contain it?"""
"686","686/988- From Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyyah who said: ""He is not wise who does not treat with kindness the one whom he cannot avoid associating with; until Allah grants him relief or a way out."""
"687","687/890 From Al-Bara' ibn 'Azib, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Whoever grants a loan of a milking animal(1) or guides someone to a street(2)—or he said: a path—will have a reward equal to freeing a slave."""
"688","688/891- From Abu Dharr, attributing it to the Prophet (he said: then he said after that: I do not know except that he attributed it to the Prophet): ""Pouring from your bucket into your brother's bucket is charity, commanding good and forbidding evil is charity, your smiling in your brother's face is charity, removing a stone, thorn, or bone from the people's path is charity for you, and guiding a man in a land of misguidance is charity."""
"689","689/892- From Ibn Abbas; that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""May Allah curse the one who leads a blind man away from the path."""
"690","690/894 From Anas, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Whoever raises two girls until they reach maturity, I and he will enter Paradise like these two,"" and Muhammad [ بن عبد العزيز] gestured with his index and middle fingers."
"691","691/895 From Anas: Two things for which punishment is hastened in this world: oppression and severing the ties of kinship."
"692","692/897 From Abu Huraira; that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""My allies on the Day of Resurrection are the righteous, even if there is a closer lineage than lineage. So let not people come to me with deeds, while you come with the world carried upon your necks, and you say: O Muhammad! And I will say thus and thus: No,"" and he turned away to both his sides."
"693","693/898 Ibn Abbas said: ""I do not see anyone acting upon this verse: 'O mankind, indeed We have created you from male and female' until he reached: 'Indeed, the most noble of you in the sight of Allah is the most righteous of you' [الحجرات: 13] . A man says to another man: I am more noble than you! But no one is more noble than another except by the fear of Allah."""
"694","694/899- From Ibn Abbas: ""What do you consider as nobility? Allah has clarified nobility, so the most noble of you in the sight of Allah is the most pious among you. What do you consider as lineage? The best of you in lineage is the best of you in character."""
"695","695/900 From Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""Souls are like recruited soldiers; those that recognize one another will come together, and those that do not recognize one another will differ."""
"696","696/901 From Abu Huraira who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Souls are like recruited soldiers; those that recognize one another will come together, and those that do not recognize one another will differ."""
"697","697/902 From Abu Huraira who said: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: ""While a shepherd was among his sheep, a wolf attacked and took a sheep from him. The shepherd pursued it, and the wolf turned to him and said: 'Who will look after it on the day of the wild beasts? It has no shepherd other than me.'"" The people said: Glory be to Allah! The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""I believe in that; I and Abu Bakr and Umar.""(1)."
"698","698/903 From Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, was at a funeral, and he took something and began to poke with it in the ground. Then he said: ""There is not one among you except that his place in the Fire and his place in Paradise has been written."" They said: O Messenger of Allah! Should we not rely on what has been written for us and leave off action? He said: ""Act! For everyone will be facilitated for that for which he was created."" He said: ""As for the people of happiness, they will be facilitated for the deeds of happiness, and as for the people of misery, they will be facilitated for the deeds of misery."" Then he recited: 'As for he who gives and fears Allah, and believes in the best...' the verses [الليل: 5-7] ."
"699","699/905 From Abdullah ibn Mughaffal al-Muzani who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade al-khadhf (flinging small stones with the fingers), and said: ""It does not kill game, nor does it harm the enemy, but it puts out the eye and breaks the tooth."""
"700","700/906 From Abu Huraira, he said: The people were overtaken by wind on the road to Mecca while Umar was performing Hajj—it became intense, so Umar said to those around him: ""What is the wind?"" But they did not reply with anything! So I urged my mount and caught up with him. I said: It has reached me that you asked about the wind? And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: ""The wind is from the spirit of Allah; it comes with mercy and it comes with punishment, so do not curse it, but ask Allah for its good and seek refuge from its evil."""
"701","701/907- From Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani; he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, led us in the morning prayer at al-Hudaybiyyah after a night rain had fallen. When the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, finished, he turned to the people and said: ""Do you know what your Lord has said?"" They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: ""This morning, some of My servants have become believers in Me and some disbelievers. As for those who said: 'We have been given rain by the grace and mercy of Allah,' they are believers in Me and disbelievers in the stars. As for those who said: 'We have been given rain by such-and-such a star,' they are disbelievers in Me and believers in the stars."""
"702","702/909 From Abdullah [ هو ابن مسعود] who said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Tiyarah is shirk, but none of us (is free from it), yet Allah removes it by reliance (on Him)."""
"703","703/910 From Abu Huraira who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""There is no superstition (2), and the best of it is optimism."" They said: And what is optimism? He said: ""A good word that one of you hears."""
"704","704/911 From Abdullah [ هو ابن مسعود] , from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""The nations were presented to me at the season during the days of Hajj, and I was impressed by the great number of my Ummah; they had filled the plain and the mountain. They said: O Muhammad! Are you satisfied? He said: Yes, O Lord! He said: With these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning; they are those who do not seek ruqya, nor cauterize, nor believe in omens, and upon their Lord they rely."" Ukasha said: So pray to Allah to make me among them. He said: ""O Allah, make him among them."" Then another man said: Pray to Allah to make me among them. He said: ""Ukasha has preceded you to it."""
"705","705/913-(Sahih) From Anas, from the Prophet, peace be upon him: ""There is no contagion and no omen, but I am pleased by a good augury; a good word."""
"706","706/914- (Sahih li-ghayrih) from Hayyah [ بن حابس ] al-Tamimi; that his father informed him, that he heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: ""There is nothing in the haamah(1), and the truest omen is optimism, and the evil eye is real."""
"707","707/915-(Hasan li-ghayrihi) From Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib: That the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, in the year of al-Hudaybiyyah, when Uthman ibn Affan mentioned that Suhayl had been sent to him by his people, so they made peace with him, on the condition that he would return from them that year, and leave it for them the following year for three [days], the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said when he came. It was said: Suhayl has come. He said, ""May Allah make your matter easy."" And Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib had met the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him."
"708","708/917 (Sahih) From Sahl ibn Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If there is any bad omen in anything, it is in the woman, the horse, and the dwelling."""
"709","709/918-(Hasan) From Anas ibn Malik who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah! We were in a house where our numbers were many and our wealth was abundant. Then we moved to another house, and our numbers decreased and our wealth decreased. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Return it, or leave it, for it is blameworthy."" Abu Abdullah said: There is some scrutiny regarding its chain of transmission."
"710","710/919-(Sahih) From Abu Huraira, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who said: ""Indeed, Allah loves sneezing and dislikes yawning. So if one sneezes and praises Allah, it is a duty upon every Muslim who hears him to respond with a supplication. As for yawning, it is only from Satan [ فإذا تثاءب أحدكم/ 928] , so let him repel it as much as he can. If he says: 'Haah,' Satan laughs at him."""
"711","711/921- From Abu Huraira, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""If one of you sneezes [ أحدكم/927] , let him say: Alhamdulillah (praise be to Allah). If he says [الحمد لله] , then his brother or companion should say to him: May Allah have mercy on you. If he says to him: May Allah have mercy on you, then let him say [هو] : May Allah guide you and rectify your condition."" Abu Abdullah said: The most authentic narration in this chapter is this hadith."
"712","712/923-(Sahih) From Ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""Four are due from a Muslim to a Muslim: he visits him when he is sick, attends his funeral when he dies, answers him when he invites, and blesses him when he sneezes."""
"713","713/924- (Sahih) From Al-Bara' ibn 'Azib who said: ""The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded us with seven things and forbade us from seven. He commanded us to visit the sick, to follow the funerals, to respond to the sneezer, to fulfill the oath, to help the oppressed, to spread peace, and to answer the invitation. And he forbade us from gold rings, silver vessels, Mayathir, Qassiy, Istabraq, Dibaaj, and silk."""
"714","714/929-(Authentic chain) From Abu Jamrah who said: I heard Ibn Abbas say, ""If you sneeze: May Allah protect us and you from the Fire(1). May Allah have mercy on you."""
"715","715/930-(Sahih) From Abu Huraira who said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, when a man sneezed and praised Allah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said to him: ""May Allah have mercy on you."" Then another sneezed, and he did not say anything to him. He said: O Messenger of Allah! You responded to the other but did not say anything to me. He said: ""He praised Allah, and you remained silent."""
"716","716/931- Narrated Anas: Two men sneezed in the presence of the Prophet, peace be upon him. He said ""Yarhamuk Allah"" to one of them, but did not say it to the other. The latter said, ""You said it to him but did not say it to me?"" He said: ""This one praised Allah, but you did not praise Him.""(1)."
"717","717/932-(Hasan) And through another chain from Abu Huraira who said: Two men sat with the Prophet, peace be upon him, one of whom was more noble than the other. The noble one among them sneezed but did not praise Allah, so he was not given the response. The other sneezed and praised Allah, so the Prophet, peace be upon him, responded to him. The noble one said: ""I sneezed in your presence and you did not respond to me, but this other man sneezed and you responded to him!"" He said: ""This one remembered Allah, so I remembered him. You forgot Allah, so I forgot you."""
"718","718/933- From Abdullah ibn Umar: When he sneezed and it was said to him, ""May Allah have mercy on you,"" he would say: ""May Allah have mercy on us and you, and forgive us and you."""
"719","719/934- From Abdullah [ هو ابن مسعود] who said: ""When one of you sneezes, let him say: All praise is due to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And let the one who responds say: May Allah have mercy on you. And let him (the one who sneezed) say: May Allah forgive me and you."""
"720","720/935-(Sahih) From Salama [ هو بن الأكوع] who said: A man sneezed in the presence of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and he said: ""May Allah have mercy on you."" Then he sneezed again, and the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""This one has a cold."""
"721","721/937- (Authentic chain) From Mujahid; he said: A son of Abdullah ibn Umar—either Abu Bakr or Abu Umar—sneezed and said: ""Aab."" Ibn Umar said: ""And what is 'Aab'? Indeed, 'Aab' is the name of a devil among the devils; he placed it between the sneeze and the praise."""
"722","722/939- (Sahih) From Abu Huraira who said: ""Say 'Yarhamuk Allah' to him once, twice, and three times; whatever is after that is just a cold."""
"723","723/940- (Sahih) From Abu Musa who said: The Jews would sneeze in the presence of the Prophet, peace be upon him, hoping that he would say to them: ""May Allah have mercy on you,"" but he would say: ""May Allah guide you and set your affairs right."""
"724","724/941- (Sahih) From Abu Burda who said: I entered upon Abu Musa – while he was in the house of [ابنته] (1) Umm al-Fadl bint al-Abbas – and I sneezed, but he did not respond to my sneeze. She sneezed, and he responded to her. I informed my mother, and when he came to her, she confronted him and said: My son sneezed and you did not respond to him, but she sneezed and you responded to her. He said to her: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""If one of you sneezes and praises Allah, then respond to him; but if he does not praise Allah, then do not respond to him."" Your son sneezed and did not praise Allah, so I did not respond to him; she sneezed and praised Allah, so I responded to her. She said: You did well."
"725","725/943 (Sahih) From Mu'adh who said: I was the companion rider of the Prophet, peace be upon him, and he said: ""O Mu'adh!"" I said: At your service and your pleasure. Then he said the same three times: ""Do you know what is Allah's right upon the servants? [قلت: لا، قال: حق الله على العباد] That they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him."" Then he went on for a while and said: ""O Mu'adh!"" I said: At your service and your pleasure. He said: ""Do you know what is the right of the servants upon Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, if they do that? That He will not punish them."""
"726","726/944 (Sahih) From Abdullah ibn Ka'b—who was the guide of Ka'b among his sons when he became blind—said: I heard Ka'b ibn Malik narrate his story when he stayed behind from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, during the expedition of Tabuk, and Allah accepted his repentance: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, announced Allah's acceptance of our repentance when he prayed the dawn prayer, so people came to me in groups, congratulating me on the repentance, saying: ""May the repentance of Allah upon you be blessed for you,"" until I entered the mosque, and there was the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, with people around him. Then Talha ibn Ubayd Allah stood up and hurried toward me until he shook my hand and congratulated me. By Allah, no man from the Muhajirun stood up to me except him; I will never forget this for Talha."
"727","727/945- From Abu Sa'id al-Khudri: That some people submitted to the judgment of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh, so he was sent for, and he came riding a donkey. When he approached near the mosque, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Bring your best, or your leader."" Then he said: ""O Sa'd! These people have submitted to your judgment."" Sa'd said: ""My judgment upon them is that their fighting men be killed and their women and children be taken captive."" The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""You have judged with the judgment of Allah,"" or he said: ""You have judged with the judgment of the King."""
"728","728/946 (Sahih) From Anas who said: ""There was no person more beloved to them to look at than the Prophet, peace be upon him, and when they saw him they would not stand up for him(5), because they knew how much he disliked that."""
"729","729/947 (Sahih) From Aisha, Mother of the Believers, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I never saw anyone among the people whose speech, conversation, or sitting resembled the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, more than Fatima. She said: And whenever the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, saw her coming, he would welcome her, then stand up for her(1), kiss her, then take her by the hand and bring her to sit in his place. And whenever the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, came to her, she would welcome him, then stand up for him [فأخذت بيده/971] and kiss him. And she entered upon the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, during his illness in which he passed away, and he welcomed her and kissed her, then spoke to her privately, and she wept! Then he spoke to her privately again, and she laughed! So I said to the women: I used to think she had some superiority over women, but she is just like other women! While she was crying, suddenly she laughed! So I asked her: What did he say to you? She said: If I were to tell, I would be spreading secrets(2)! When the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, passed away, she said: He confided to me and said: ""I am going to die,"" so I wept, then he confided to me again and said: ""You will be the first of my family to join me,"" so I was pleased with that, and it made me happy."
"730","Jabir reported: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, became ill, so we prayed behind him while he was sitting, and Abu Bakr was conveying his takbir to the people. The Prophet turned to us and saw us standing, so he gestured to us and we sat down. We prayed following his prayer while sitting. When he finished, he said: ""You were about to do as the Persians and Romans do; they stand before their kings while they (the kings) are seated. Do not do so. Follow your imams: if he prays standing, then pray standing; and if he prays sitting, then pray sitting.""(1)"
"731","731/949- From Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet, peace be upon him, who said: ""If one of you yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth; for the devil enters into it."""
"732","732/950 (Authentic chain, Mawquf) From Ibn Abbas who said: ""When one yawns, let him place his hand over his mouth; for it is from the Shaytan."""
"733","733/952 (Sahih) From Anas ibn Malik who said: ""The Prophet, peace be upon him, used to enter upon Umm Haram, daughter of Milhan, and she would feed him. She was the wife of Ubadah ibn al-Samit. She fed him, and began to comb his head for lice. He slept, then woke up laughing."""
"734","734/953 (Hasan li-ghayrihi) from Qais ibn Asim al-Sa'di who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, and he said: ""This is the chief of the people of the tents."" So I said: O Messenger of Allah! What wealth is there upon which there is no liability from a claimant or a guest? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Good wealth is forty, and more is sixty, and woe to the owners of hundreds, except for one who gives the noble, grants the abundant, and slaughters the fat one, so he eats and feeds the content and the beggar."" I said: O Messenger of Allah! How noble are these morals; no one settles in a valley where I am because of the abundance of my camels. He said: ""How do you deal with giving?"" I said: I give the young and I give the mature. He said: ""How do you deal with the grant?"" I said: I grant the she-camel. He said: ""How do you deal with the breeding camel?"" I said: People come in the morning with their ropes, and no man is prevented from taking a camel, leading it away, and keeping it as long as he wishes, until he returns it himself. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Is your wealth more beloved to you, or the wealth of your heirs?"" [قال : مالي] . He said: ""You have from your wealth only what you eat and consume, or what you give and send forth, and the rest is for your heirs."" I said: Certainly, if I return, I will reduce their number. When death approached him, he gathered his sons and said: O my sons! Take from me, for you will not take from anyone more sincere to you than me: Do not wail over me, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, was not wailed over, and I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, forbidding wailing. Shroud me in the clothes in which I used to pray, and appoint your elders as leaders, for if you appoint your elders as leaders, your father will always have a successor among you, but if you appoint your young ones, your elders will be belittled by people and they will lose respect for you. Improve your livelihood, for in it is sufficiency from seeking from people, and beware of begging, for it is the last resort of a man’s earning. When you bury me, level the earth over my grave, for there used to be some disputes between me and this clan of Bakr ibn Wa'il: minor quarrels, and I do not trust that a foolish person might do something that would bring shame upon your religion."
"735","735/955 (Sahih) From Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, came to him and Fatima, the daughter of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, at night and said: ""Will you not pray?"" I said, O Messenger of Allah! Our souls are in the hand of Allah, so if He wills to wake us, He will wake us! The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, turned away and did not reply to me. Then I heard him as he was leaving, striking his thigh and saying: ""But man is, more than anything, argumentative."" [الكهف: 54]"
"736","736/956 (Sahih) From Abu Huraira, he said: I saw him striking his forehead with his hand and saying: O people of Iraq! Do you claim that I lie about the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him! Should you have the benefit and I bear the sin? I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, say: ""If the thong of one of your sandals breaks, let him not walk in the other until he repairs it."""
"737","737/957 (Sahih) From Abu Al-‘Aliyah; Al-Bara’, who said: ‘Abdullah ibn Al-Samit passed by me, so I placed a chair for him and he sat. I said to him: “Ibn Abi Ziyad has delayed the prayer, what do you command?” He struck my thigh—a blow, I think he said, that left a mark—then said: “I asked [خليلي/954] Abu Dharr as you have asked me, and he struck my thigh as I struck yours, then said: [أتيت النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم بوضوء، فحرك رأسه، وعض على شفتيه! قلت: بأبي أنت وأمي، آذيتك؟ قال: "" لا ولكنك تدرك أمراء – أو أئمة- يؤخرون الصلاة لوقتها"". فقلت: فما تأمرني؟ قال: ] ‘Pray the prayer at its time; then if you catch it with them, pray [with them], and do not say (in another narration: and do not ever say): I have already prayed, so I will not pray.’”"
"738","738/(958/1) From Abdullah ibn Umar: That Umar ibn al-Khattab set out with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, with a group of his companions towards Ibn Sayyad, until they found him playing with the boys in the enclosure of Banu Maghala, and at that time Ibn Sayyad was nearing puberty. He did not notice until the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, struck his back with his hand, then said: ""Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?"" He looked at him and said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of the unlettered! Ibn Sayyad said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, pressed him, then said: ""I believe in Allah and His Messenger."" Then he said to Ibn Sayyad: ""What do you see?"" Ibn Sayyad said: A truthful one and a liar come to me. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""The matter has been confused for you."" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""I have concealed something for you."" He said: It is ad-dukh. He said: ""Be gone, for you will not go beyond your rank."" Umar said: O Messenger of Allah! Do you permit me to strike his neck? The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""If he is him, you will not be given power over him, and if he is not, then there is no good for you in killing him."""
"739","739/(958/2)- Abdullah ibn Umar said: After that, the Prophet, peace be upon him, and Ubayy ibn Ka'b al-Ansari went one day to the palm trees where Ibn Sayyad was. When the Prophet, peace be upon him, entered, he began to shield himself behind the trunks of the palm trees, while he was hearing something from Ibn Sayyad before seeing him. Ibn Sayyad was lying on his bed, wrapped in a blanket, murmuring something. The mother of Ibn Sayyad saw the Prophet, peace be upon him, as he was shielding himself behind the trunks of the palm trees, and she said to Ibn Sayyad: ""O Saf! (that was his name), this is Muhammad."" So Ibn Sayyad stopped. The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""If she had left him, it would have become clear."""
"740","740/(958/3) (Sahih) Abdullah said: The Prophet, peace be upon him, stood among the people and praised Allah as He deserves, then mentioned the Dajjal and said: ""I am warning you about him, and there has not been a prophet except that he warned his people. Indeed, Noah warned his people, but I will say to you about him something that no prophet has said to his people: You should know that he is one-eyed, and that Allah is not one-eyed."""
"741","741/959 (authentic chain) From Jabir who said: ""When the Prophet, peace be upon him, was in a state of janabah, he would pour three handfuls of water over his head."" Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad said: By Allah! My hair is more than that! He (Jabir) struck [ جابر] his hand on Al-Hasan's thigh and said: O son of my brother! The hair of the Prophet, peace be upon him, was more than your hair and better."
"742","742/960 (Sahih) From Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, fell from a horse in Medina onto the trunk of a palm tree, and his foot was dislocated. So we used to visit him in the upper room of Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her. We came to him while he was praying sitting, so we prayed standing. Then we came to him another time while he was praying the obligatory prayer sitting, so we prayed behind him standing. He gestured to us to sit down. When he finished the prayer, he said: ""If the imam prays sitting, then pray sitting; and if he prays standing, then pray standing. Do not stand while the imam is sitting, as the Persians do with their great ones."""
"743","743/961 (Sahih) [جابر] said: A son was born to so-and-so(1) from the Ansar, and he named him Muhammad. The Ansar said: We will not give you the kunya of the Messenger of Allah. Until we sat in the road asking him about the Hour. He said: ""You have come to me asking me about the Hour?"" We said: Yes. He said: ""There is no soul that will reach one hundred years."" We said: A son was born to so-and-so from the Ansar and he named him Muhammad, and the Ansar said: We will not give you the kunya of the Messenger of Allah. He said: ""The Ansar have done well. Name (your children) with my name, but do not use my kunya."""
"744","744/962 (Sahih) From Jabir ibn Abdullah: That the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, passed through the market entering from some part of al-‘Aliyah—and the people were around him—so he passed by a dead, deformed kid [ميت] , and he took hold of it by its ear, then said: ""Which of you would like to have this for a dirham?"" They said: We would not like to have it for anything; what would we do with it? He said: ""Would you like to have it for yourselves?"" They said: No. (He said that to them three times.) They said: No, by Allah! If it were alive, it would be a defect in it that it is deformed (and the deformed is the one without ears), so how about when it is dead? He said: ""By Allah, the world is more insignificant to Allah than this is to you."""
"745","745/963 (Sahih) From ‘Uti bin Dumrah who said: I saw with my father a man who called himself by the slogans of the Jahiliyyah, so my father told him to bite it – and he did not use a euphemism – so his companions looked at him. He said: It is as if you find this strange?! He said: I do not fear anyone in this matter ever; I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: ""Whoever calls himself by the slogans of the Jahiliyyah, tell him to bite it and do not use a euphemism."""
"746","746/965 (Sahih) From Abu Musa: He was with the Prophet, peace be upon him, in a garden from the gardens of Medina, and in the hand of the Prophet, peace be upon him, was a stick with which he was striking between the water and the mud—(4) then a man came seeking permission to enter, so the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""Open for him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise."" So I went, and it was Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, so I opened for him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then another man sought permission to enter, so he said: ""Open for him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise."" And it was Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, so I opened for him and gave him glad tidings of Paradise. Then another man sought permission to enter—and he was reclining, so he sat up—and said: ""Open for him, and give him glad tidings of Paradise after a trial that will befall him, or will occur."" So I went, and it was Uthman, so I opened for him and informed him of what he had said. He said: Allah is the One whose help is sought."
"747","747/966 (Sahih al-Isnad) from Salamah ibn Wardān who said: I saw Anas ibn Malik shaking hands with the people, so he asked me: Who are you? I said: A freed slave of Banu Layth. So he wiped over my head three times and said: ""May Allah bless you."""
"748","748/967 (Authentic chain, Mawquf) From Anas ibn Malik who said: When the people of Yemen came, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: ""The people of Yemen have arrived, and they are more tender-hearted than you."" They were the first to introduce handshaking."
"749","749/968 (Authentic chain, Mawquf) from Al-Bara’ ibn ‘Azib who said: ""Part of the completeness of greeting is that you shake hands with your brother."""
"750","750/970- (Hasan) From Jabir ibn Abdullah: That a report reached him from a man among the companions of the Prophet, peace be upon him, so I bought a camel and traveled for a month until I reached al-Sham. There was Abdullah ibn Unais, so I sent word to him that Jabir is at the door. The messenger returned and said: Jabir ibn Abdullah? I said yes. He came out and embraced me. I said: A hadith has reached me that I have not heard; I feared that I might die or you might die. He said: I heard the Prophet, peace be upon him, say: ""Allah will gather the servants—or the people—bare, uncircumcised, and buhma."" I said: What is buhma? He said: ""They have nothing with them. Then He will call them with a voice that will be heard by those far away—I think he said: just as it is heard by those near: I am the King. It is not fitting for anyone from the people of Paradise to enter Paradise while someone from the people of the Fire seeks from him a wrong."" And it is not fitting for anyone from the people of the Fire to enter the Fire while someone from the people of Paradise seeks from him a wrong."" I said: How? When we come to Allah bare and buhma? He said: ""With good deeds and bad deeds."""
